'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''sixteenth series''' with a launch show on 8 September 2018 on [[BBC One]], and the first live show on 22 September. [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned as hosts, while [[Zoe Ball]] returned to host ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' on [[BBC Two]]. [[Shirley Ballas]], [[Darcey Bussell]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returned as judges. On 20 October, actor [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] stood in as a guest judge to cover for Tonioli.<ref name=":11">{{cite web |last=Green |first=Alex |date=19 October 2018 |title=Strictly Come Dancing: What you need to know ahead of this weekend |url=https://www.independent.ie/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-this-weekend-37437863.html |access-date=20 October 2018 |work=[[Irish Independent]]}}</ref>

In this series, three new dance styles were introduced — [[Contemporary dance|contemporary]], [[Jazz dance|theatre/jazz]], and [[Street dance|street/commercial]] — as part of a new category called "couple's choice".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2018-09-08/strictly-come-dancing-new-couples-choice-category/|title=Strictly Come Dancing introduces brand new 'Couple's Choice' category|first=Ellie|last=Harrison|work=[[Radio Times]]|date=8 September 2018|access-date=8 September 2018}}</ref>

[[Stacey Dooley]] and [[Kevin Clifton]] were announced as the winners on 15 December 2018,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2018/12/15/strictly-come-dancing-2018-final-live-will-joe-sugg-stacey-dooley/|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2018 final, live: Stacey Dooley and Kevin Clifton crowned champions despite finishing bottom of scoreboard|work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]|first=Michael|last=Hogan|date=15 December 2018|access-date=15 December 2018}}</ref> while [[Joe Sugg]] and [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Faye Tozer]] and [[Giovanni Pernice]], and [[Ashley Roberts]] and [[Pasha Kovalev]] were the runners-up.

