The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

==Professional dancers==
On 30 May 2018, the list of professionals returning for the sixteenth series was revealed. Professionals from the last series who did not return included [[Brendan Cole]] and [[Chloe Hewitt]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/strictly-come-dancing/news/a848738/brendan-cole-axed-strictly-come-dancing/|title=Brendan Cole reveals he has been axed from Strictly Come Dancing|last=McCreesh|first=Louise|date=30 January 2018|work=[[Digital Spy]]|access-date=30 May 2018}}</ref> [[Graziano Di Prima]], [[Luba Mushtuk]], and [[Johannes Radebe]] replaced them.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/2c041434-fe0e-4566-bf45-b9f9e8ddfde7|title=We reveal our biggest pro-dancer line-up ever! As a trio of outstanding dancers join the show|date=30 May 2018|publisher=BBC|access-date=30 May 2018}}</ref> Mushtuk and Radebe did not have celebrity partners; however, Di Prima did.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://metro.co.uk/2018/08/27/why-doesnt-neil-jones-ever-have-a-partner-on-strictly-come-dancing-7886517/|title=Why doesn't Neil Jones ever have a partner on Strictly Come Dancing?|last=Westbrook|first=Caroline|date=30 August 2018|work=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|access-date=1 September 2018}}</ref><ref name=couples>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/ea3aa382-918c-46a5-b20e-55fc00752165|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – It's time to meet your 2018 couples!|publisher=BBC One|date=8 September 2018|access-date=8 September 2018}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured fifteen celebrity contestants. On 13 August 2018, the first three celebrities announced to be participating in the series were [[Katie Piper]], [[Faye Tozer]], and [[Danny John-Jules]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/8d258664-104e-4ff1-a970-26e072e8ad24|title=Katie Piper is our first Strictly star of 2018!|date=13 August 2018|work=BBC News |access-date=13 August 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/ccad03e5-db11-4192-a49e-e8d681aadbfe|title=Steptacular news... Faye Tozer is joining our Strictly 2018 line-up!|date=13 August 2018|work=BBC News |access-date=21 August 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/84126ef9-a064-4614-8ed7-4ebde401a29f|title=Danny John-Jules is ready for Strictly 2018!|date=13 August 2018|work=BBC News |access-date=21 August 2018}}</ref> Celebrity reveals continued across that month before concluding on 21 August on ''[[Good Morning Britain (2014 TV programme)|Good Morning Britain]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.com/tv/strictly-come-dancing/news/a864432/strictly-come-dancing-2018-line-up-complete-chucky-venn-susannah-constantine/|title=Strictly Come Dancing completes its line-up with 14th and 15th stars|date=21 August 2018|work=Digital Spy|access-date=21 August 2018}}</ref><ref name=couples/>
